      "header": "Phone booking loses patients before the visit",
      "text": "I called three times and gave up. **By the time someone answered, I had to get back to work.**",
      "speaker": "Patient, 40s, Riverside",
      "source_id": "s2",
      "emphasis": true
     },
     {
      "header": "Reminders do not reach people",
      "text": "The reminder came as a letter after the date. **A text the day before would have done it.**",
      "speaker": "Patient, 60s, Oak Park",
      "source_id": "s2"
     },
     {
      "header": "Online booking changes the habit",
      "text": "Since I can book on my phone at night, **I have not missed one appointment this year.**",
      "speaker": "Patient, 30s, Hillcrest (books online)",
      "source_id": "s2"
     }
    ]
   },
   "so_what": "Fixing booking and reminders addresses the reasons patients give; demand for care is not the problem",
   "so_what_style": "line"
  },
